# Patent Claim

**Claim 1.** A (meth)acryloyl compound represented by the following formula (A):

**Formula (A):**

$$
\left[ \text{CH}_2=\text{C}(R^{1A})-\text{C}(=\text{O})-\text{O} \right]_{p}-Z-\left[ X-\left( R^1 \right)_{k} \right]_{m}\left( \text{H} \right)_{n}
$$

wherein:

**X** each independently represents a divalent linking group selected from the group consisting of a single bond, an oxygen atom (–O–), a sulfur atom (–S–), a carbonyl group (–C(=O)–), an ester group (–C(=O)O– or –OC(=O)–), an amide group (–C(=O)NH– or –NHC(=O)–), a urethane group (–NHC(=O)O– or –OC(=O)NH–), a sulfonyl group (–SO₂–), a substituted or unsubstituted alkylene group having 1 to 12 carbon atoms, a substituted or unsubstituted arylene group having 6 to 14 carbon atoms, and a combination of two or more thereof, wherein one or more –CH₂– groups in said alkylene group may be replaced by –O–, –S–, or –NH–;

**Z** represents an (m+p)-valent linking group derived from an aliphatic, alicyclic, aromatic, or heterocyclic compound having 1 to 30 carbon atoms, said linking group optionally containing one or more heteroatoms selected from oxygen, nitrogen, and sulfur, and optionally being interrupted or substituted by one or more of an ether bond, an ester bond, a carbonate bond, and a urethane bond;

**R¹** each independently represents a substituent selected from the group consisting of a hydrogen atom, a halogen atom, a hydroxyl group, a cyano group, a substituted or unsubstituted alkyl group having 1 to 12 carbon atoms, a substituted or unsubstituted alkoxy group having 1 to 12 carbon atoms, a substituted or unsubstituted aryl group having 6 to 14 carbon atoms, and a (meth)acryloyloxy group;

**R¹ᴬ** each independently represents a hydrogen atom or a methyl group;

**k** represents an integer of 0 to 4, and when k is 2 or more, the plural R¹ groups may be the same or different from one another;

**m** represents an integer of 1 to 6;

**n** represents an integer of 0 to 5;

**p** represents an integer of 1 to 6; and

with the proviso that the sum (m + p) is an integer of 2 to 8, and the sum (m + n) corresponds to the total valency available on Z other than that occupied by the (meth)acryloyloxy-containing groups.

---

*Note: The specific structural formula, valency relationships, and substituent ranges shown above are illustrative. In actual practice these should be adapted to match the precise chemical structure disclosed in your specification and supported by your working examples.*

# Claim 1 — (Meth)acryloyl Compound

**1.** A compound represented by Formula (I):

$$\text{[CH}_2=\text{C(R}^1)-\text{C(=O)-O-]}_m\text{—L—[X]}_n$$

wherein:

**R¹** is, independently at each occurrence, a hydrogen atom or a methyl group;

**L** is an *m*+*n* valent linking group having a valence of from 2 to 8, selected from the group consisting of:

- (a) a substituted or unsubstituted, linear, branched, or cyclic aliphatic hydrocarbon group having from 1 to 20 carbon atoms;
- (b) a substituted or unsubstituted aromatic hydrocarbon group having from 6 to 18 carbon atoms;
- (c) a group in which one or more of the carbon atoms of the groups defined in (a) or (b) is replaced by a heteroatom selected from oxygen, nitrogen, and sulfur; and
- (d) a single bond, provided that *m*+*n* equals 2;

**X** is, independently at each occurrence, a substituent selected from the group consisting of a hydroxyl group, a halogen atom, a substituted or unsubstituted alkyl group having from 1 to 6 carbon atoms, a substituted or unsubstituted alkoxy group having from 1 to 6 carbon atoms, a (meth)acryloyloxy group, an amino group, a cyano group, a nitro group, and a substituted or unsubstituted aryl group having from 6 to 12 carbon atoms;

**m** is an integer of from 1 to 6;

**n** is an integer of from 0 to 6; and

the sum of *m* and *n* is an integer of from 2 to 8, and corresponds to the valence of the linking group L;

wherein, when any of the foregoing groups is substituted, the optional substituents are independently selected from a halogen atom, a hydroxyl group, an alkyl group having from 1 to 4 carbon atoms, and an alkoxy group having from 1 to 4 carbon atoms.

---

*Drafting notes: The above establishes (i) the divalent-to-octavalent range of the linking group L, (ii) an explicit closed list of allowable substituents for both X and the optional substituents, and (iii) integer ranges for each variable (m, n) together with the linking-relationship constraint (m + n = valence of L). Adjust the specific carbon-number ranges, valence limits, and substituent enumerations to conform to your worked embodiments and to preserve support and enablement under the applicable jurisdiction.*

**Claim 1.** A crosslinkable (meth)acrylate compound represented by the following general formula (I):

**General Formula (I):**

$$\left[\ \mathrm{CH_2{=}C(R^1){-}C({=}O){-}O{-}}\right]_m\!\!-\!\!Z\!\!-\!\!\left[\,(A)_k\,\right]_p\!\!-\!\!(R^2)_n$$

wherein:

**R¹** represents a hydrogen atom or a methyl group;

**Z** represents a linking group selected from a linear, branched, or cyclic aliphatic hydrocarbon group having 1 to 12 carbon atoms, an aromatic hydrocarbon group having 6 to 14 carbon atoms, or a combination thereof, said linking group optionally containing 1 to 4 heteroatoms selected from oxygen, nitrogen, and sulfur in its main chain;

**A** represents a divalent connecting moiety selected from –O–, –C(=O)–, –C(=O)O–, –OC(=O)–, –NH–, –S–, or a straight-chain or branched alkylene group having 1 to 6 carbon atoms;

**R²** each independently represents a substituent selected from the group consisting of:

&nbsp;&nbsp;(a) a hydrogen atom;
&nbsp;&nbsp;(b) a halogen atom selected from fluorine, chlorine, bromine, and iodine;
&nbsp;&nbsp;(c) a linear or branched alkyl group having 1 to 8 carbon atoms;
&nbsp;&nbsp;(d) an alkoxy group having 1 to 6 carbon atoms;
&nbsp;&nbsp;(e) a functional group selected from hydroxy, carboxy, cyano, nitro, amino, epoxy, and glycidyloxy; and
&nbsp;&nbsp;(f) a vinylphenylmethyl-substituted hydroxy group represented by the partial formula:

$$-\mathrm{O{-}CH_2{-}C_6H_4{-}CH{=}CH_2}$$

&nbsp;&nbsp;wherein the vinyl group is positioned at the ortho, meta, or para position of the phenylene ring;

**m** is an integer of 1 to 3;
**n** is an integer of 0 to 5;
**k** is an integer of 0 to 2; and
**p** is 0 or 1;

with the proviso that at least one **R²** is the vinylphenylmethyl-substituted hydroxy group of (f) when p is 0, and that the total number of substituents does not exceed the available valences of the linking group **Z**.

---

**Dependent claims (optional):**

**Claim 2.** The crosslinkable (meth)acrylate compound according to claim 1, wherein R¹ is a methyl group, m is 2, and at least one R² is the vinylphenylmethyl-substituted hydroxy group defined in (f).

**Claim 3.** The crosslinkable (meth)acrylate compound according to claim 1, wherein Z is a phenylene or naphthylene group and A is –C(=O)O– or –O–.

**Claim 4.** The crosslinkable (meth)acrylate compound according to claim 1, wherein n is 1 to 3 and each halogen-bearing R² is a fluorine atom.
